2. Method
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   D. Afchar, G. Meseguer-Brocal, K. Akesbi, R. Hennequin,
   "A Fourier Explanation of AI-music Artifacts", ISMIR 2025 (best paper).
   https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.19108

   The insight this whole project rests on: the transposed-convolution
   (deconvolution) layers that generative audio models use to upsample
   latents back to sample rate leave regularly-spaced peaks in the frequency
   domain. The artifact is a property of the ARCHITECTURE, not of the
   training data or the weights, which is why so small a classifier works.

   Deezer's own reference implementation is CC BY-NC-4.0 and is therefore NOT
   used, vendored, or derived from here. This project's extractor was written
   from the published method and from the MIT implementation in (1).


